/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO/DebateAI-V3/docs/missions/2026-08-14-model-evaluator/requirements/Requirements.md:354:### FR-6.1 Persist per-call tokens per model
/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO/DebateAI-V3/docs/missions/2026-08-14-model-evaluator/requirements/Requirements.md:356:**Requirement.** Cost for the evaluator is **token-ledger derived**. This mission (ticket 08, fed by ticket 01) SHALL implement persistent per-call token (and optional vendor cost) capture per model from what each path actually exposes:
/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO/DebateAI-V3/docs/missions/2026-08-14-model-evaluator/requirements/Requirements.md:358:- Shared loss point today: CLI relays drop usage at `parseCompletion` / relay-core response rebuild.
/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO/DebateAI-V3/docs/missions/2026-08-14-model-evaluator/requirements/Requirements.md:359:- Smallest capture direction (findings recommendation): widen shared CLI completion with optional usage; emit standard `usage` on the relay HTTP response; persist into `raw_artifact.metadata_json` (or later queryable columns) without inventing tokens.
/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO/DebateAI-V3/docs/missions/2026-08-14-model-evaluator/requirements/Requirements.md:360:- vLLM already returns `usage.prompt_tokens/completion_tokens/total_tokens` in body; recover/surface them when that path is selected (FR-0.6).
/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO/DebateAI-V3/docs/missions/2026-08-14-model-evaluator/requirements/Requirements.md:361:- Paths that report nothing stay **`usage: null` / unmetered** — never estimated.
/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO/DebateAI-V3/docs/missions/2026-08-14-model-evaluator/requirements/Requirements.md:365:1. **In scope under ticket 08:** after capture implementation, for at least one path that already receives usage on the wire (grok and/or claude CLI envelope fields per findings), a completed call stores non-null usage inspectable per model identity.
/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO/DebateAI-V3/docs/missions/2026-08-14-model-evaluator/requirements/Requirements.md:366:2. Unmetered paths store explicit null/absent usage; relative-cost aggregation excludes them from token/cost sums and surfaces `unmetered_call_count` (or equivalent) per model.
/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO/DebateAI-V3/docs/missions/2026-08-14-model-evaluator/requirements/Requirements.md:371:### FR-6.2 Relative cost signal for seat-share (normalized)
/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO/DebateAI-V3/docs/missions/2026-08-14-model-evaluator/requirements/Requirements.md:373:**Requirement.** From metered calls, derive a **relative cost** signal per model (not absolute currency in product UI). Seat-share allocator (FR-8) reads this signal. No manual cost ranks. Because paths expose **heterogeneous units** (e.g. `total_cost_usd` on claude/grok envelopes vs token counts on vLLM), the derivation MUST document and test a **normalization basis** (per-path unit → common relative-cost scale). Raw token totals alone MUST NOT rank a free local model as more expensive than a paid subscription path solely because token counts are larger.
/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO/DebateAI-V3/docs/missions/2026-08-14-model-evaluator/requirements/Requirements.md:377:1. Given two models with different measured usage on comparable windows, relative cost ranks them using the documented normalization — without human-entered cost ranks.
/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO/DebateAI-V3/docs/missions/2026-08-14-model-evaluator/requirements/Requirements.md:378:2. Unit test covers at least one cross-unit case (USD-cost path vs token-count path) showing the documented rule, not raw token comparison alone.
/Users/vladmihaimiron/Documents/DebateAIRO/DebateAI-V3/docs/missions/2026-08-14-model-evaluator/requirements/Requirements.md:379:3. Quality tiers remain existing casual/standard/high-stakes + depth knobs — metering does not invent payment tiers.
